 "drivingQuestion": "What is the widow doing with the orphans' property?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "R' Yirmeya sets the mishna in a widow who is an heiress.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_batra.144a.3",
   "daf": "144a",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "הָאִשָּׁה שֶׁהִשְׁבִּיחָה אֶת הַנְּכָסִים – הִשְׁבִּיחָה לָאֶמְצַע. אִשָּׁה בְּנִכְסֵי יַתְמֵי מַאי עֲבִידְתַּהּ? אָמַר רַבִּי יִרְמְיָה: בְּאִשָּׁה יוֹרֶשֶׁת.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: With regard to «a wife who enhanced the property» of her deceased husband, «she enhanced» it so that the profit goes «to the middle.» The Gemara asks: «What is» the deceased’s «wife doing with» the «orphans’ property?» What rights does she have to the property? «Rav Yirmeya said:» The mishna is referring «to a wife» who is «an heiress,» e.g., if she were the daughter of her husband’s brother, and both brothers died without leaving sons, in which case she inherits in her father’s stead."
  }
 ],
